Evidence: hs2 batches of 25 chapters, which worked for China-2023 test
queries (18-53s), are unreliable for at least one other year/flow: exports
2013-12 batch 1 (chapters 01-25) and batch 2 (chapters 26-50) each timed
out after 60s x 3 internal retries (ReadTimeout), then correctly fell back
to per-chapter requests, each of which succeeded in 1-12s. To reduce wasted
retry time (each failed 25-chapter batch costs about 180s before falling
back), HS2_BATCH_SIZE is reduced from 25 to 10 chapters per request for the
rest of this acquisition. This does not change correctness, only request
count and expected wall-clock time; the per-chapter fallback path is
unchanged and already proven.
