25.2s). exports batch 1 failed with a 500 server error after 152.9s
(not a timeout); exports batch 2 also failed at the 180s ceiling
(second consecutive batch failure), so hs2_batches_disabled flipped to
true partway through 2016 exports, per-chapter for the remainder of that
batch and every chapter after. Year 2016 total archive time: about 12.6
minutes (faster than 2014/2015's ~30+ minutes each, since imports got the
fast batched path). From year 2017 onward, HS2 batching stays disabled
(one-way switch, state.json hs2_batches_disabled=true) and every chapter,
both flows, is fetched one at a time (proven reliable throughout).
Increasing archive chunk-size to 3 years per invocation from here since
per-year behavior is now uniform and predictable.
